Subject: Forum/est

My, yes, The Forum(TM) does have impressively hard-sell tactics,
doesn't it?  I walked out of their Introductory Night because they
were so obnoxious.

But they do seem to be useful -- they provide a structure in which
people receive positive feedback that they are not immoral for wanting
what they want, and consistent pressure to attempt to achieve what
they want.  From a game-theoretical (economic/evolutionary) point of
view, it is interesting how they work -- The Forum and the social
group that it provides for you has no reason to inhibit you from
getting what you want, unlike your family, co-workers, etc., who will
be the ones to suffer your newly self-assertive personality.  The only
thing that The Forum wants to impose on you is your continued
subscription to The Forum seminars, but that may be a reasonable price
to pay for the psychological support you receive from them.

Dale

